ridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: reproduced the complete four-token sentinel vocabulary, the three allowed value-position forms, the exact eight-term same-line suppression list, and concrete fail/pass examples in the plan. Also added explicit verification of the two existing direct-consumer test files identified by G1G2. No source edits or tests have started; ticket remains open pending a signed review.","timestamp":1785192471891325001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD checkpoint: added focused cross-surface regressions first and confirmed 7 initial failures. Implemented one shared pure parser, wired standalone clarity, then wired deterministic P1. Added two follow-up red/green edge controls for fenced AC continuations and checkbox-prefixed sentinel assignments. Current verification: tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py 24 passed; existing direct consumers plus broader plan-review unit coverage 142 passed. Review advisories were resolved as immediate trigger-word proximity and whole-word suppression matching. TokenSave reduced initial code-navigation context by approximately 42,505 tokens.","timestamp":1785193121531081001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification complete on the final candidate: focused clarity-floor suite 25 passed; direct existing-consumer and broader plan-review suites 142 passed; `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed across 381 source files; canonical `make test` passed with 7,305 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, 13 existing multiprocessing deprecation warnings in 26m44s. No source changed during the canonical full-suite run.","timestamp":1785195533538464001}],"created_at":1785191917835107001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7fcda645-db59-4431-9094-6c7e535c3c59","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e759-c562-e233-4108"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe accepted clarity analysis on ticket e759-c562-e233-4108 identified two structurally unambiguous plan defects that the current length-and-heading heuristic does not reject: empty parsed Acceptance Criteria items and unresolved sentinel assignments in active execution sections. Standalone clarity and deterministic P1 must enforce the same floor without changing ticket-type exemptions or the legacy compatibility score.\n\n## Approach\n- Add one pure shared plan-structure helper. Inside the exact `## Acceptance Criteria` section, recognize standard `- [ ]` and `- [x]` checklist items, join every continuation line until the next checklist item or H2 heading, and mark an item defective only when the joined body is whitespace-empty.\n- In exact active `## Approach`, `## Scope`, `## Testing`, and `## Acceptance Criteria` sections, scan case-insensitively for the sentinel tokens `TBD`, `TODO`, `FIXME`, and `???`. Ignore fenced code and inline backtick code. A sentinel fires only when it starts a line or bullet, follows `:` or `=`, or follows the word `is`, `remains`, or `left`.\n- Suppress a sentinel match when its same line contains a removal or negation term from this exact case-insensitive list: `no`, `zero`, `remove`, `delete`, `reject`, `forbid`, `must not`, `without`. Thus `Backend: TBD`, `TODO — decide cache`, and `status remains ???` fail; `NO stale TODO`, `Remove TODO markers`, and ``mention `TODO` as an example`` pass.\n- Wire the shared result into standalone `clarity_check_compute` and plan-review `p1_readiness_shape`, preserving the existing clarity score as compatibility coverage.\n- Add focused behavior tests before implementation, including historical negative controls and agreement between the two gate surfaces.\n\n## Scope\n- Add `src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py` for the shared structural parser and hard-floor result.\n- Update `src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py` to apply the result to standalone clarity.\n- Update `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py` to emit blocking P1 findings for the same defects.\n- Add `tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py` for focused unit and cross-surface regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the focused clarity-floor tests during the red-green cycle.\n- Re-run existing direct-consumer coverage in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py` and `tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py`.\n- Run the repository lint, typecheck, and full test gates after the focused suite is green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A standard Acceptance Criteria checkbox whose fully joined body is whitespace-empty fails standalone clarity.\n- [ ] A checkbox with a blank first line and a nonblank wrapped continuation passes the nonempty-item rule.\n- [ ] Each specified sentinel-as-value form in an exact active execution section fails standalone clarity.\n- [ ] Fenced code does not trigger the sentinel rule.\n- [ ] Inline code does not trigger the sentinel rule.\n- [ ] Ordinary prose mentions do not trigger the sentinel rule.\n- [ ] Each specified same-line removal or negation assertion suppresses the sentinel rule.\n- [ ] Plan-review P1 blocks on an empty joined checkbox body.\n- [ ] Plan-review P1 blocks on an unresolved sentinel assignment.\n- [ ] Plan-review P1 passes the historical `NO stale TODO` negative control.\n- [ ] Focused tests, direct-consumer tests, lint, typecheck, and the full repository test suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py","reason":"shared deterministic plan-structure parser and clarity floor"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py","reason":"standalone clarity gate integration"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","reason":"blocking P1 readiness integration"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_clarity_floor.py","reason":"focused parser and cross-surface regression tests"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"33d2b0dd-075b-4196-bafb-bf6985e3a28e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["clarity","plan-review","gates"],"ticket_id":"9385-4ba8-ec93-44c3","ticket_type":"task","title":"Enforce deterministic clarity floors for executable plans","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5657ae45-ff2e-4412-ae1a-86e299cbc73a","2a24ab3b-0d46-4645-b1a9-42e0d38d8696","7fcda645-db59-4431-9094-6c7e535c3c59","0a22d107-3a3d-4623-a95e-4558c665f158","0d677359-29cf-4dbf-8191-2fe31f82524e","7097cba4-15cf-4e5f-a924-bdaf0b0bdf3e","33d2b0dd-075b-4196-bafb-bf6985e3a28e","bca91d27-82ac-4ea4-9b33-60c4686e89ad","fdc62180-4464-4830-8a68-e9bcc8cf12b8","be839fcb-e516-46f2-afa1-eac483cbf27c","64b249b1-b071-46d5-94c1-ffa23c63b058"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785195533538464002,"uuid":"4d6d2c3b-eb9f-4bd6-8bdb-38026c928d16"}